<title>USA: Kent State University, Ohio, $37 mln priced.</title>
<headline>Kent State University, Ohio, $37 mln priced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>John Nuveen &amp; Co said Tuesday that it tentatively priced $37.5 million of Kent State University, Ohio, general receipts bonds, Series 1996, with a top yield of 5.75 percent in 2028.</p>
<p>The bonds are book entry and MBIA insured.</p>
<p>The bonds are rated Aaa by Moody's Investors Service and AAA by Standard &amp; Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>The bonds are dated 10/15/1996 and due 5/1.</p>
<p>The first coupon is 5/1/1997.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected 11/12/1996 and the award is expected 10/30/1996.</p>
<p>The bonds are callable 11/1/2006 at 102.00 and declining to par 11/1/2008 at 100.00.</p>
